{"content":[{"c":["JOEL (P",{"c":["erson"],"sourceClass":"lc","t":"span"},")"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":[" 1. Levite from the family of Kohath. He was Azariah’s son and an ancestor of Elkanah, the father of Samuel the prophet (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.1.1","r":"1Sam.1.1","rawR":"1Sam.1.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.1.1","value":"1Sam.1.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 1:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.36","r":"1Chr.6.36","rawR":"1Chr.6.36","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.36","value":"1Chr.6.36"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:36"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 2. Oldest son of Samuel the prophet. He and his brother Abijah so corrupted the office of judge that the elders increased their demands for a king (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.8.2-5","r":"1Sam.8.2-5","rawR":"1Sam.8.2-5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.8.2-5","value":"1Sam.8.2-5"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 8:2-5"},"). He was the father of Heman the singer (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.33","r":"1Chr.6.33","rawR":"1Chr.6.33","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.33","value":"1Chr.6.33"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:33"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.15.17","r":"1Chr.15.17","rawR":"1Chr.15.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.15.17","value":"1Chr.15.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"15:17"},"). His name has been mistakenly translated “Vashni” in the ",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," in ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.28","r":"1Chr.6.28","rawR":"1Chr.6.28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.28","value":"1Chr.6.28"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chronicles 6:28"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 3. Prince from one of the Simeonite families that emigrated to the valley of Gedor (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.4.35","r":"1Chr.4.35","rawR":"1Chr.4.35","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.4.35","value":"1Chr.4.35"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 4:35"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 4. Member of Reuben’s tribe (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.5.4,8","r":"1Chr.5.4,8","rawR":"1Chr.5.4,8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.5.4,8","value":"1Chr.5.4,8"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 5:4, 8"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 5. Chief of Gad’s tribe residing in Bashan (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.5.12","r":"1Chr.5.12","rawR":"1Chr.5.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.5.12","value":"1Chr.5.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 5:12"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 6. Third of Izrahiah’s four named sons and a chief of Issachar’s tribe in David’s time (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.7.3","r":"1Chr.7.3","rawR":"1Chr.7.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.7.3","value":"1Chr.7.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 7:3"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 7. Nathan’s brother and one of David’s mighty men (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.11.38","r":"1Chr.11.38","rawR":"1Chr.11.38","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.11.38","value":"1Chr.11.38"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 11:38"},"). He is alternately called Igal the son of Nathan in ",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.23.36","r":"2Sam.23.36","rawR":"2Sam.23.36","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.23.36","value":"2Sam.23.36"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Samuel 23:36"},". ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Igal_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Igal_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Igal_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Igal #2"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 8. Levite from the family of Gershon who participated in the royal procession that brought the ark of God to Jerusalem during David’s reign (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.15.7-11","r":"1Chr.15.7-11","rawR":"1Chr.15.7-11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.15.7-11","value":"1Chr.15.7-11"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 15:7-11"},"). He may have administered the treasuries of the temple in Jerusalem (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.26.22","r":"1Chr.26.22","rawR":"1Chr.26.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.26.22","value":"1Chr.26.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 26:22"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 9. Pedaiah’s son, who acted as tribal chieftain over the west half of Manasseh’s tribe during David’s reign (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.27.20","r":"1Chr.27.20","rawR":"1Chr.27.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.27.20","value":"1Chr.27.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 27:20"},")"],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["10. Levite from the family of Kohath who assisted in King Hezekiah’s reform of the temple in Jerusalem (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.29.12","r":"2Chr.29.12","rawR":"2Chr.29.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.29.12","value":"2Chr.29.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 29:12"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["11. Nebo’s son, who was encouraged by Ezra to divorce his foreign wife during the postexilic period (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.10.43","r":"Ezra.10.43","rawR":"Ezra.10.43","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.10.43","value":"Ezra.10.43"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 10:43"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["12. Zicri’s son and the supervisor of 128 Benjaminites who moved to postexilic Jerusalem (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.11.9","r":"Neh.11.9","rawR":"Neh.11.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.11.9","value":"Neh.11.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 11:9"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["13. Prophet who wrote the second book of the Minor Prophets. Little is known about him except that he was Pethuel’s son (",{"href":"?bref=Joel.1.1","r":"Joel.1.1","rawR":"Joel.1.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Joel.1.1","value":"Joel.1.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jl 1:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Acts.2.16","r":"Acts.2.16","rawR":"Acts.2.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.2.16","value":"Acts.2.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 2:16"},"). ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=JoelBookof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"JoelBookof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"JoelBookof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Joel, Book of"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"JoelPerson","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Sm 1:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.1.1","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.1.1","sourceRefExa